{"actor": "opencode", "data": {"argv": ["tools/origin", "task", "complete", "T-0055", "--summary", "A claim published from inside the session that made it. taskremote.claim committed the claim then called push, which refuses a dirty tree; an open session guarantees one, so the refusal named the session's own record and said commit or revert it. The claim stayed local and unpushed, so no other VM could see it - the exclusivity the command exists to provide was not in force - and each retry appended another claim line to the append-only ledger (three identical ones for T-0053), while the retry's own advice named sync land, which refuses the same dirty tree. The claim commit now carries the open session's record via sessionflow.session_owned_paths, and foreign uncommitted work refuses the claim before anything is written; release took the same treatment. Falsified both ways and on a clone of this repository's own history. Defect 21, D044, F023; 548 tests green, preflight 0.", "--evidence", "tools/originlib/claimpublish.py", "--evidence", "tools/originlib/taskremote.py", "--evidence", "tests/test_claim_in_session.py", "--evidence", "FAILURES-findings-5.md"], "cwd": "/home/ubuntu/think-free", "duration_ms": 893, "exit_code": 0, "log": "sessions/2026-10-04-041-repair-the-red-base-state-md-over-the-li/commands.log", "log_line_end": 257, "log_line_start": 250, "redactions": [], "summary": "$ tools/origin task complete T-0055 --summary A claim published from inside the session that made it. taskremote.claim committed the claim the"}, "duration_ms": 893, "exit_code": 0, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "command", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 33, "session": "2026-10-04-041-repair-the-red-base-state-md-over-the-li", "ts": "2026-10-04T16:03:28+00:00"}
